::

Section action buttons are icon-only (G3 pass, WP-N3 08-11): View on web (external-link), Connect domain (globe), Edit (edit glyph), Link Task (＋) — old labels carry as `aria-label`, verbs unchanged; every glyph resolves in the registry, no fallback circles.

Section notes: Web is absent without a `public_url`; Demo absent shows "No in-app demo yet — ask Surfy to build this app's site."; Code is gated on `repoProvisioned` — the rows-as-tree + fenced code block stand in for the deferred `nav-tree` and `code-editor` (this is the mockup's surface-code section, folded in); Deployments status colors by contains-match (succe→green, fail/error→red, run/progress→orange, else muted); PR rows carry the accent "Surfy" badge when agent-opened.

Android section (round 6, 08-19): the WHOLE section is gated on an Android target existing for the app (the Ultra/Studio capability gate rides server-side — no target, no section, exactly the Web-absent idiom). Target row = package name over `Target · next versionCode {n}`. Release rows, newest first, cap 20: `v{versionCode} · {versionName}` over `{created} · {track}` — track absent renders "not uploaded" (the WP-1 built-not-uploaded state). `downloadAab` rows carry the REAL AAB href only when the bundle bytes exist; a release without its AAB renders the row without the action. Build AAB (`buildAndroid`) enqueues the pipeline build — the toolbar is the section's only action; keystore export and target creation stay classic-web/settings surfaces this round. An **iOS** build/deploy section is deliberately ABSENT: no iOS build lane exists server-side yet (the shipping iOS app's own "iOS" section is the demo link, which the Demo section already carries) — authoring it here without a backend would violate the no-fake-affordances law; it lands with the mobile-deploy round.

::callout[type=note title="Renderer note — deferred"]
`web-preview` (inline sandboxed demo frame) is consciously deferred this round — the `::figure` fallback above stands in per the gaps plan. Do not add `web-preview` here.
::

## Sheets — defined once, opened from here

- **Connect domain** — `modals/connect-domain.surf` (`name=connect-domain`), via the Web section's button (`openConnectDomain`). Connect runs the in-sheet progression: Verifying DNS → DNS verified — binding → connected; certificate issues after bind.
- **Link Task** — `modals/link-task.surf` (`name=link-task`), via the Tasks section's ＋ (`openLinkTask`). Already-linked rows render checked + disabled; the sheet stays up for multi-link.
